{
    "background_story": "Delaney grew up on a rural farm, where summer days were spent helping her family harvest corn. She loved nothing more than biting into a freshly picked ear, the sweetness of the kernels bursting in her mouth. One summer, Delaney's family started a roadside stand, selling fresh produce to passing travelers. Delaney's specialty was grilling corncobs to perfection, slathering them with butter, salt, and pepper. Her corncobs became famous among locals and travelers alike, with people driving miles out of their way to taste her mouthwatering treats. As the years passed, Delaney's corncob stand became a beloved institution, symbolizing the warmth and hospitality of the rural community. Delaney's love for corncobs brought people together, fostering a sense of connection and joy that went far beyond a simple summer snack.",
